Gen 3 Remake — Engine License
Copyright (c) 2026 Dustin. All rights reserved.

This license covers the Gen 3 Remake engine: the released .apk and .love
binaries, the LuaJIT bytecode inside them, the engine source (published or
not), and the documentation. It does not cover, and grants no rights to,
any Nintendo / Creatures Inc. / GAME FREAK material — see "Third-party
content" below.

1. WHAT YOU MAY DO
   a. Download and run the official released binaries for personal,
      non-commercial use, on as many of your own devices as you like.
   b. Write, use, and distribute mods that load through the engine's mod
      API (Wiki → Home). Mods you write are yours, under whatever terms
      you choose, provided they contain no engine code or bytecode and no
      material extracted from a ROM.
   c. Stream, record, screenshot, and write about the engine freely. A
      link to the official repository is appreciated but not required.
   d. Report bugs and suggest changes via the official Issues tracker.

2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO
   a. Copy, redistribute, re-host, mirror, or bundle the binaries or
      bytecode, in whole or in part, anywhere other than the official
      repository's Releases page. Link to Releases instead.
   b. Decompile, disassemble, deobfuscate, or otherwise reverse-engineer
      the bytecode or binaries, or reuse any part of the engine — code,
      bytecode, decoders, data layouts, or documentation — in any other
      project.
   c. Sell the engine, charge for access to it, place it behind a
      paywall, bundle it with paid products, show advertising alongside a
      redistributed copy, or solicit donations in its name. "Non-
      commercial" here means no money changes hands in connection with
      the engine, in either direction.
   d. Distribute the engine together with a ROM, a save file containing
      ROM-derived data, or instructions for obtaining a ROM.
   e. Remove or alter this license, the DISCLAIMER, or any copyright or
      attribution notice.

3. THIRD-PARTY CONTENT
   The engine ships no Nintendo assets. At runtime it reads graphics,
   audio, text, and game data from a Pokémon Emerald ROM that you supply.
   Pokémon, Pokémon Emerald, and all related names, characters, and data
   are trademarks and copyrights of Nintendo, Creatures Inc., and GAME
   FREAK Inc. This license grants no rights whatsoever in that material.
   Your right to possess and use the ROM is governed by the law of your
   own jurisdiction and is entirely your responsibility.

   Behaviour is reproduced with reference to the pret/pokeemerald
   decompilation (https://github.com/pret/pokeemerald), whose contributors
   are gratefully acknowledged. No pokeemerald source is included.

   Bundled font: DejaVu Sans, under its own license (see
   src/ui/fonts/DejaVuSans-LICENSE.txt in the release).

